a thing that I find very fascinating  about one piece is the way it portrays  morality compared to other mangas  especially in Shonen manga despite the  obvious efforts of some authors there is  a clear line between good and evil and  in characters that are meant to be in a  morally gray zone usually end up on one  end of the spectrum sooner or later the  decisive factor for this are often the  moral values these characters hold and  most fights are based on clashes between  morally good and morally bad ideologies  a reliable example for this might be  boku no hero academia the manga is based  on the conflict between heroes that are  trying to protect their good values and  the villains who follow their own  twisted and bad ideologies what stands  out at the center of such storytelling  is the clear opposition of good and evil  in the individual convictions of  characters the ultimate display of this  being the fight of all might against all  for one such stories make it relatively  easy and clear to pick which side is the  morally right and which is the morally  wrong but while there are many mangas of  this kind that you can easily consider  as great one piece does something  different even if it feels slightly  counterintuitive at first glance from  the back of your head it surely enough  feels like the stories also build upon a  conflict of good versus bad ideologies  but if I told you to take a moment and  come up with a character that holds  purely evil values in the sense that  their goal is actually to do evil how  many characters could you actually come  up with there's actually a strong  argument that this number would actually  be very close to zero because in fact  the Wampus world does not have a  Voldemort or so on that seek dominion  over all and now you might think well  what about Blackbeard but what actually  is his ideology simple Blackbeard values  and aims for the exact same thing as our  main character Luffy freedom and freedom  in itself surely is not a concept that  most people would deem as morally wrong  in fact all major players in one piece  hold ideals that cannot be put into two  categories like wrong or good by  themselves Luffy and Blackbeard price  freedom above all else the Marines value  order and justice and white beat values  family none of these ideals are  fundamentally evil but they still come  into conflict with each other now  what I'm describing here is the concept  of moral pluralism basically it says  that people aren't simply good or bad  based on the ideal stay hold and the  different ideologies can morally be  acceptable and still contradict each  other this applies to our world as well  where we often tend to look down on  people who share opposite views and  ideals than us and mark them is bad and  ignorant right from the start this view  of morality is what makes one piece so  different from many other stories now  based on this it might make you wonder  if the argument here is that there's  actually no good or no evil in one piece  but that's not the case in fact not  seeing someone like Blackbeard or kind  of as evil would render the whole plot  of the story meaningless so the argument  here much rather is that ODIs  understanding of good and evil is not  based on values and ideals but rather on  something different so let's try this  let's look at a few examples the Marines  in general value order and justice this  ideology is interpreted very differently  by very different people while the likes  of garb and Sengoku see it as their duty  to protect the innocent and the weak by  being gentle and respectful and trying  to be genuine even in the treatment of  their enemies a kind of an Lucci  slaughter and destroy knowledge in order  to keep the very same ideal both the  white beard pirates and the donkey heart  pirates value family over everything but  while white beard views all of his crew  equally as his children and will go to  any lengths to protect them the  flamingos gave a kind of hierarchy to  his subordinates and while his system as  family he also sees it as his right to  make use of them to his benefit lastly  let's take a look at Luffy and  Blackbeard both follow the ideologies of  freedom and dreams both have a very  similar crew and yet Luffy wants to  share this dream with his crew and help  those in need  while black bead uses these ideals as a  justification to murderers on crewmate  and slaughter his way through the grand  line with the worst people imaginable as  such it is not a coincidence that there  are so many parallels between the two  characters now what these examples  should help illustrate is that good or  evil do not come from values that people  hold but rather from the way they  interpret and act upon them the way you  affect those around you by trying to  reach your ideals is what really  determines the morality of a person to  Oda this is what makes Blackbeard such a  unique villain  what makes one piece such a fascinating  story compared to other mangas now I  would like to hear your opinion on this  matter what do you think makes a  character good or bad and other  characters with truly evil ideals in one  piece and what do you think for example  about Kaito is his ideal and goal  revenge is it death and would that be  morally wrong to strive for share your  thoughts on this admittedly very  philosophical topic in the comments  below if you liked this video don't  forget to like share and subscribe to be  notified for any future content of mine  or dislike don't share and unsubscribe  it's a free world people I hope this  year on next time and until then have a  great week  [Music]  [Music]
 

